Check A: Are the metrics returning data?
timeseries {req = sum(dt.service.request.count),
            fail = sum(dt.service.request.failure_count, default:0)},
           by:{dt.entity.service}
| fieldsAdd reqs = arraySum(req), fails = arraySum(fail)
| summarize services = count(), withTraffic = countIf(reqs > 0), withFailures = countIf(fails > 0)

Check B: Which lookup filter drops the rows?
fetch dt.entity.service
| fields id, Service = entity.name, tags
| expand tag = tags
| fieldsAdd tag = toString(tag)
| summarize apmids = collectDistinct(if(contains(tag, "APMID:"), splitString(tag, "APMID:")[1],
                       else: if(contains(tag, "APPID:"), splitString(tag, "APPID:")[1]))),
            by:{id, Service}
| fieldsAdd apmidCount = arraySize(apmids), apmid = apmids[0]
| filter in(apmid, array($ClaimsApps))
| summarize services = count(), single = countIf(apmidCount == 1), multi = countIf(apmidCount > 1)
